; celltext.eval - the editor's inspector text speaks the player's language
; (code-review C107). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 26, on its scratch world.
;
; A right-click on a square of the editor map (`editor inspect`) says what is on
; it - "Cell 23, 9: floor, 1 monster" - on the editor's message line, which also
; goes to dungeon.log as `editor: ...`. The words round the numbers were English
; spliced into a localised pattern, so a German editor read "Zelle 23, 9: floor,
; 1 monster"; and the projectile card's units ("pts", "m/s", "m") and its payload
; line ("burn 1.5/s for 5.0s (25%)") were English in every language. The judge
; rebuilds each line from the .lang file itself and demands it word for word, and
; refuses a key a file lacks (the game shows it raw) rather than match it.
;
;   --- de ---       under `lang de`: a wall block; the warrior's square (one
;                    monster); a square given a skeleton and two barrels (the
;                    plural prop key), one given one pot (the singular) and 7,5,
;                    where the judge authors two skeletons into the scratch
;                    arena's .ent (the plural monster key: the editor places one
;                    monster a square); then crypt1, BROWSED from eval_arena - the
;                    remote branch, which says the square's base word alone, even
;                    of crypt1's skeleton at 10,4. And `editor cell` on two of
;                    them: the dev readout, which stays English in any language.
;   --- de shot ---  the card of a lit torch the leader threw before the switch,
;                    held in the air by `timescale 0`: its rows as the labels
;                    show them (`editor projectile: <label> = <value>`).
;   --- en ---       the same squares in English, and
;   --- en shot ---  the same torch's card.
;   --- ru shot ---  the card once more under `lang ru`: de.lang words the speed
;                    and range units as English does ("m/s", "m"), so only a
;                    language that words them otherwise ("м/с", "м") can show
;                    those rows were not left in English.
;
; `lang` persists to settings.ini (it is the Settings dropdown's path), so this
; ends on `lang en`; the judge puts the developer's settings.ini back as well.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
editor
editor place monsters skeleton 5 5
editor place decorations barrel 5 5
editor place decorations barrel 5 5
editor place decorations pot 9 5
throw torch_lit
lang de
echo --- de ---
editor inspect 0 0
editor inspect 23 9
editor inspect 5 5
editor inspect 9 5
editor inspect 7 5
editor inspect off
editor cell 0 0
editor cell 5 5
levels view crypt1
editor inspect 0 0
editor inspect 10 4
levels view eval_arena
echo --- de shot ---
editor inspect 14 12
editor inspect off
lang en
echo --- en ---
editor inspect 0 0
editor inspect 23 9
editor inspect 5 5
editor inspect 9 5
editor inspect 7 5
editor inspect off
levels view crypt1
editor inspect 0 0
editor inspect 10 4
levels view eval_arena
echo --- en shot ---
editor inspect 14 12
editor inspect off
lang ru
echo --- ru shot ---
editor inspect 14 12
editor inspect off
lang en
echo --- end ---
